From d1dba67bccdcb5dc9f9060e57721c8a99e4a8661 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:18:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sdat: a wave is decoded as it plays, not whole at its first
 note

decode_swav decoded a whole SWAV at its first note, inside the mix: on the
3DS port under the lock the game's sound frame waits for (Azahar's Old 3DS
mode held it 24-46 ms for the intro's first notes). Now the head is decoded
then and the mixer asks for the rest as it reaches it (sd_wave_fill); a trim
finishes the waves still playing. sd_waves_stats counts the decodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 port/hal/sdat/mixer.cpp |   6 ++
 port/hal/sdat/sdat.cpp  | 127 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 port/hal/sdat/sdat.h    |  16 ++++-
 3 files changed, 108 insertions(+), 41 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/hal/sdat/mixer.cpp b/port/hal/sdat/mixer.cpp
